.TH BOOTSTASH 5 "September 2026" "bootstash" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
bootstash \- operator config, dist defaults, and OIDC secrets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/default/bootstash
.br
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist
.br
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
bootstashd reads dist defaults
.RI ( /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist ),
then
.IR /etc/default/bootstash ,
then
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json .
Later source wins for scalars. If the operator file mentions
.B BIND
at all, its
.B BIND=
lines replace the packaged listen list (several
.B BIND=
lines in
.I /etc/default/bootstash
append to each other). The secrets file cannot change
.BR BIND .
.PP
.I /etc/default/bootstash
is a conffile and ships with commented
.BR DATA ,
.BR BIND ,
.BR PUBLIC_URL ,
and
.BR ADMIN_USERS .
Add only keys that differ from
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist .
Do not copy the full dist file into
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.B bootstash provision-google
does not write this file.
If the operator deletes this conffile,
.B dpkg
will not restore it;
configure copies
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default
back if the path is missing. It does not enable the unit.
If the daemon is already running it
.BR try-restart s
after the cert copy; if it is down it starts only when
.B bootstash check-config
would pass (same as
.BR bootstashd \-t ).
First install without a Google client id stays down.
It prints remaining steps (daemon not started or not enabled on
boot, no Google client id, loopback
.BR BIND ,
no copied certs).
.PP
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
is the Google Web application client JSON
.B bootstash provision-google
installs. It is not a conffile. Do not put
.BR BIND ,
.BR PUBLIC_URL ,
or other operator keys there.
.PP
Format:
.B KEY=value
lines,
.B #
comments, no shell expansion. Mode
.BR 0640 ,
owner
.BR root:bootstash
so the daemon user can read them. The daemon reads these files itself;
do not use systemd
.BR EnvironmentFile= .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B PUBLIC_URL
Browser-facing URL (scheme and host, no trailing slash).
Used for OIDC redirects, cookies, and CSRF Origin checks.
When unset, the daemon uses
.B CERT_NAME
(or
.B hostname \-f
if none) and the first TCP
.B BIND
port, with scheme
.B https
when cert files are present.
Ports 80 and 443 are omitted.
.B localhost
is not used.
Write this when the phone’s URL is not that host.
.TP
.B BIND
Repeatable listen spec:
.IR where:port
with optional
.B /ipv4
or
.BR /ipv6 .
.I where
may be
.BR * ,
an address, a CIDR, an interface name, or
.BR unix://path .
Port 0 is rejected. Unix sockets are HTTP only.
A CIDR is expanded to
.B local
addresses in that prefix, not a client allowlist.
Loopback is skipped unless the prefix is loopback.
If no address matches at start, the daemon refuses to run; on reload
it keeps the previous listeners.
A missing interface is retried at start and kept on reload.
.TP
.B TLS_CERT / TLS_KEY
If both are set, TCP binds use HTTPS with these files.
When unset, the daemon uses
.I /etc/bootstash/certs/<name>/fullchain.pem
and
.I privkey.pem
if both exist.
.I name
is
.BR CERT_NAME
(see below).
Do not point these at
.IR /etc/letsencrypt/live
.RB ( User=bootstash
cannot read it).
.TP
.B CERT_NAME
Let’s Encrypt lineage / directory under
.IR /etc/bootstash/certs .
When unset, the hook (which can read
.IR live/ )
chooses
.BR live/ $(hostname -f)
or the only
.I live/
lineage; the daemon then sees that
.I certs/<name>/
pair. Several lineages and no
.B CERT_NAME
:
.B sync
prints the list and copies nothing.
A successful detect inserts
commented
.B CERT_NAME=
and
.B PUBLIC_URL=
hints (the URL the daemon would derive; does not rewrite
operator keys). The daemon still derives both unless those
lines are uncommented.
Not an ACME client.
.TP
.B DATA
Data volume. Default
.IR /var/lib/bootstash .
.TP
.B OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
Google web OAuth client. Client ID is required to start.
These keys may appear in
.I /etc/default/bootstash .
The secrets file
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
is the JSON the Google console downloads
.RB ( web.client_id
/
.BR web.client_secret ).
.B bootstash provision-google
installs that file
.RB ( 0640
.BR root:bootstash ).
JSON secrets win if both are set. A KEY=value secrets file is still
read.
.TP
.B OIDC_CRYPTO
Optional HMAC key (at least 32 bytes, or hex). If unset, a key is created
under
.IR $DATA/state/crypto.key .
.TP
.B PAM_SERVICE
PAM service name. Default
.BR bootstashd
(file
.IR /etc/pam.d/bootstashd ).
The
.B bootstash
CLI does not use PAM.
.TP
.B MAX_UPLOAD
Upload size cap in bytes (suffixes such as
.B 32MiB
are accepted). Default 32MiB.
.TP
.B SHARED_WRITABLE
If
.BR 1 ,
allow HTTP writes into
.IR shared/ .
Default off.
.TP
.B UNIX_GROUP
Group for Unix sockets. Default
.BR bootstash .
.TP
.B ADMIN_USERS
Comma- or space-separated PAM usernames treated as operators (the
admin seam). Default empty: nobody. SIGHUP re-reads the list. v1
grants no extra HTTP powers; later admin routes will use this list.
Not a Unix group and not an application user table.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/bootstash
Directory for helper-written secrets and copied TLS files
.RB ( 0750
.BR root:bootstash ).
Created by tmpfiles or the helper. Do not use systemd
.BR ConfigurationDirectory= .
.TP
.I /etc/bootstash/certs/<name>
.I fullchain.pem
and
.I privkey.pem
readable by
.BR bootstash
.RB ( 0640
.BR root:bootstash ).
Filled by
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/letsencrypt-deploy
(linked from
.IR /etc/letsencrypt/renewal-hooks/deploy/bootstash ).
Certbot runs that hook on issue and renew for the
chosen lineage. The package runs
.B letsencrypt-deploy sync
on configure (prints if nothing matches). See
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/QUICKSTART.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstashd (8),
.BR bootstash (8)
